diff --git a/docs/privacy-security.md b/docs/privacy-security.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b69d714
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-security.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Privacy and security operations
+
+Status: implemented controls, independent audit pending. Automated scans are not an independent audit.
+
+## Data inventory
+
+| Data | Purpose | Storage and retention | Deletion |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Random session ID | Associate a requested reading list | HttpOnly, Strict, Secure production cookie; 24h | DELETE reading-list endpoint expires cookie |
+| Up to 100 article IDs | User-requested bookmarks | Process memory; timers remove within 24h of last write; 10,000 session cap | DELETE or remove last bookmark |
+| Search terms | Local article filtering | React memory only | Close page |
+| IP and URL | Hosting/network delivery | Operator-managed infrastructure | Configure hosting log lifecycle |
+
+The session driver deliberately avoids disk and backups. Restarts discard all lists. Multiple instances do not share sessions: use a single instance or sticky routing. Before adopting shared storage, require encryption, access controls, native TTL deletion and documented retention. Cookie expiry may precede list expiry after a later list edit; the server still purges the orphaned list.
+
+## Integration register
+
+| Service | Decision | Data flow |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Cloud Functions analytics and ads | Removed | None |
+| Cloud Functions registration/login | Disabled pending independent review | None; credential inputs removed |
+| Google Fonts | Removed; system serif fallback | None |
+| External article image hosts | Replaced with bundled editorial images | None |
+| Hosting operator | Required deployment review | Connection metadata; establish log retention and access |
+
+## Independent audit procedure
+
+Before re-enabling any personal-data provider, commission an independent reviewer and record: provider and owner, purpose and lawful basis, exact data fields, destinations and subprocessors, applicable contractual terms, retention, deletion/export mechanism, encryption in transit and at rest, access controls, incident handling, current independent assessment evidence (including scope and date), findings, remediation proof, reviewer and approval date. Keep sensitive evidence in a restricted repository, referenced by ID here. Reject missing or stale evidence. Reassess at least annually and after material provider/data-flow changes. No provider currently has recorded approval.
+
+Scope the application audit to storage/cookies, CSRF, request limits, CSP and security headers, supply chain, operational access/logs and deletion. Track findings by owner and due date and independently retest fixes. Never label a dependency scan or this document as third-party certification.
+
+## Deployment requirements
+
+Terminate HTTPS, restrict direct HTTP origin access, preserve security headers and ensure the adapter sees the public HTTPS URL for HSTS and same-origin checks. Disable request body logging at proxies; redact cookies and credentials. Set minimum operational log retention and access policies with the hosting owner. Remove any legacy `.astro/sessions` files and backups from earlier deployments under the operator's deletion procedure; new sessions use memory only. Audit any platform-injected scripts.
+
+The header CSP blocks remote connections, frames, fonts and images. Astro additionally supplies per-page script/style hashes in the rendered response CSP, as described in [Astro's configuration documentation](https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/configuration-reference/#securitycsp). Do not replace these policies with `unsafe-inline` scripts. Validate with a production build: Astro does not enable generated CSP hashes in development.
+
+Run `pnpm run test:privacy`, `pnpm run build`, and `pnpm audit` during release review. Run independent audits before integration approval and on the schedule above. Dependency audit results must be triaged and documented; registry findings can change over time.
+
+## Automated dependency review — 2026-10-20
+
+`pnpm audit` initially found two moderate advisories: Vite 7.3.6 (GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv) and postcss-selector-parser 6.0.10 (GHSA-rj75-hqrm-r3gf). Updated the Vite 7 dependency resolution and scoped a parser override to the typography plugin. The follow-up scan reports zero known advisories. Production build and privacy regression tests validate the updated dependencies. This is automated dependency review, not independent audit evidence.
